   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the young boy shown in the reference images - identity, face, hair, clothing and build come from the attached reference image, NOT from this text description.\n<Picture 1> is the FIRST frame: the empty dark room - a dark near-black room, a simple wooden table, one chair, a single bare bulb hanging directly above as the ONLY light source, casting a hard top-down shadow, everything outside the bulb's light pool fading to pure black, NO person.\n<Picture 2> is the LAST frame: the young boy shown in the reference images seated at the table, both hands resting on the table edge.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] A single continuous black & white, high contrast, fine film grain, 24fps take that animates smoothly from <Picture 1> (the empty dark room, no person) to <Picture 2> (Jaisal seated at the table). a dark near-black room, a simple wooden table, one chair, a single bare bulb hanging directly above as the ONLY light source, casting a hard top-down shadow, everything outside the bulb's light pool fading to pure black. The room, table, chair and bulb stay EXACTLY the same so the cut to the next shot is seamless. The bare bulb NEVER moves, swings, oscillates or flickers - it is a fixed, steady light source for the ENTIRE shot, including the LAST frame.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in this shot): fully_preserved - the young boy shown in the reference images. There is ONLY ONE character - the young boy shown in the reference images - NO other people, NO second person, NO duplicates, NO extra figures.\n<Picture 1> (first frame): fully_preserved - the opening frame.\n<Picture 2> (last frame): fully_preserved - the shot ENDS exactly on this frame.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe shot BEGINS from <Picture 1> (the empty dark room, no person). The bare bulb is COMPLETELY STILL (no swinging, no oscillation, no flicker, steady light); a chair scrapes across the floor; Jaisal <Subject 1> enters from the darkness, drags the chair, and sits down, hands coming to rest on the table edge. He does NOT stand, does NOT leave, is NOT duplicated. Camera: a WIDE STATIC eye-level shot (35mm), the camera is locked and does NOT move, push, drift, tilt, pan or zoom. The shot ENDS exactly on <Picture 2> (Jaisal seated at the table, hands on the table edge).\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA continuous natural ambient bed fills the ENTIRE shot with no gaps - low room tone, the faint electric hum of a bare bulb, a soft chair scrape on wood, a gentle breath, the quiet creak of the chair settling. ONLY these natural sounds, edge to edge. ABSOLUTELY NO instruments of any kind - NO guitar, NO plucked strings, NO strumming, NO strings, NO piano, NO keys, NO drums, NO beat, NO melody, NO humming, NO singing, NO voice, NO speech. The audio is PURELY ambient room sound.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: NO music of ANY kind. NO instrumental music, NO musical instruments, NO guitar, NO acoustic guitar, NO electric guitar, NO plucked strings, NO strumming, NO string instruments, NO violin, NO cello, NO piano, NO keyboard, NO drums, NO percussion, NO melody, NO tune, NO beat, NO rhythm, NO humming, NO singing, NO song, NO score, NO soundtrack, NO background music, NO ambient music, NO cinematic score, NO soundtrack bed, NO musical tone of any kind. Natural ambient sounds ONLY.\n\nnegative: color, multiple people, second person, duplicate character, extra chairs, extra figures, bright wall, white wall, cream wall, visible ceiling, text, subtitles, watermark, logo, the man standing, the man leaving, a second person, bulb swinging, bulb oscillating, bulb flickering, moving light, swinging bulb, flickering light, guitar, guitar sound, plucked strings, strumming, any instrument, any instrumental sound, melody, musical tone, humming, singing, music"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "value": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the young boy shown in the reference images - identity, face, hair, clothing and build come from the attached reference image, NOT from this text description.\n<Picture 1> is the FIRST frame: the empty dark room - a dark near-black room, a simple wooden table, one chair, a single bare bulb hanging directly above as the ONLY light source, casting a hard top-down shadow, everything outside the bulb's light pool fading to pure black, NO person.\n<Picture 2> is the LAST frame: the young boy shown in the reference images seated at the table, both hands resting on the table edge.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] A single continuous black & white, high contrast, fine film grain, 24fps take that animates smoothly from <Picture 1> (the empty dark room, no person) to <Picture 2> (Jaisal seated at the table). a dark near-black room, a simple wooden table, one chair, a single bare bulb hanging directly above as the ONLY light source, casting a hard top-down shadow, everything outside the bulb's light pool fading to pure black. The room, table, chair and bulb stay EXACTLY the same so the cut to the next shot is seamless.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in this shot): fully_preserved - the young boy shown in the reference images. There is ONLY ONE character - the young boy shown in the reference images - NO other people, NO second person, NO duplicates, NO extra figures.\n<Picture 1> (first frame): fully_preserved - the opening frame.\n<Picture 2> (last frame): fully_preserved - the shot ENDS exactly on this frame.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe shot BEGINS from <Picture 1> (the empty dark room, no person). The bare bulb swings gently; a chair scrapes across the floor; Jaisal <Subject 1> enters from the darkness, drags the chair, and sits down, hands coming to rest on the table edge. He does NOT stand, does NOT leave, is NOT duplicated. Camera: a WIDE STATIC eye-level shot (35mm), the camera is locked and does NOT move, push, drift, tilt, pan or zoom. The shot ENDS exactly on <Picture 2> (Jaisal seated at the table, hands on the table edge).\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA continuous natural ambient bed fills the ENTIRE shot with no gaps - low room tone, the faint electric hum of a bare bulb, a soft chair scrape on wood, a gentle breath, the quiet creak of the chair settling. Only these natural sounds, edge to edge.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: NO music, NO instrumental music, NO musical instruments, NO melody, NO beat, NO rhythm, NO soundtrack, NO song, NO score, NO background music, NO ambient music, NO cinematic score, NO soundtrack bed. Natural ambient sounds only - absolutely no music of any kind.\n\nnegative: color, multiple people, second person, duplicate character, extra chairs, extra figures, bright wall, white wall, cream wall, visible ceiling, text, subtitles, watermark, logo, the man standing, the man leaving, a second person"
   },
